From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anatoliy Shulika <shulikaa@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: brcmstb: enable UBUS inbound access on BCM4908

On BCM4908 the inbound (device-to-host) windows stay closed unless the
UBUS remap register has ACCESS_EN set, so an endpoint cannot reach host
memory even though the link trains and config space is readable.

Verified by reverting this change on a TP-Link Archer C2300 v1
(BCM4906): brcmfmac immediately regresses to "Timeout on response for
query command" / "dongle is not responding", because the dongle can no
longer read the host-memory msgbuf rings it is pointed at.

Signed-off-by: Anatoliy Shulika <shulikaa@icloud.com>
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-brcmstb.c
@@ -1009,8 +1009,36 @@ static void set_inbound_win_registers(st
 		 *     Do nothing.
 		 * 7712:
 		 *     All of their BARs need to be set.
+		 * 4908:
+		 *     The UBUS bridge gates inbound (device to host) access
+		 *     separately from the RC BAR itself, so the BAR alone is
+		 *     not enough: without ACCESS_EN set on the corresponding
+		 *     UBUS remap register, endpoint DMA into system memory
+		 *     never reaches DRAM.  Broadcom's own bcm963xx PCIe host
+		 *     driver does this on this SoC family, writing
+		 *     MISC_UBUS_BAR1_CONFIG_REMAP (PCIE_MISC_REGS_OFFSET +
+		 *     0x00ac, i.e. the same 0x40ac register used here) with
+		 *     MISC_UBUS_BAR_CONFIG_ACCESS_EN (BIT(0)) right after
+		 *     programming the inbound DDR BAR.
+		 *
+		 *     This went unnoticed upstream because no in-tree bcm4908
+		 *     board has a working driver for a PCIe endpoint, so only
+		 *     MMIO paths (link training, enumeration, config space)
+		 *     were ever exercised - all of which work fine with the
+		 *     gate shut.
+		 *
+		 *     Verified by reverting this change on a TP-Link Archer
+		 *     C2300 v1 (BCM4906): brcmfmac immediately regresses to
+		 *     "Timeout on response for query command" / "dongle is not
+		 *     responding", because the dongle can no longer read the
+		 *     host-memory msgbuf rings it is pointed at.
+		 *
+		 *     Only windows that are actually enabled are touched;
+		 *     brcm_pcie_get_inbound_wins() leaves BAR1 and BAR3 with a
+		 *     size of zero on this SoC and only BAR2 maps DRAM.
 		 */
-		if (pcie->cfg->soc_base == BCM7712) {
+		if (pcie->cfg->soc_base == BCM7712 ||
+		    (pcie->cfg->soc_base == BCM4908 && size)) {
 			/* BUS remap register settings */
 			reg_offset = brcm_ubus_reg_offset(i);
 			tmp = lower_32_bits(cpu_addr) & ~0xfff;
